ll prove the theorem'' describes a \emph{particular authenticated actual run}. Keeping those events separate is essential.

\textbf{Repair record from original working note.} The section structure and research question are retained. This edition (i) corrects the actual/emittable versus possibly emittable confusion in former Definition 8.1 and Theorem 8.2; (ii) makes the quotient invariant and task family explicit; (iii) adds budget-preserving simulations and a cross-budget qualification; (iv) adds mandatory BANK import checks to former Lemma 6.2; (v) specifies the first-person referent and delegation; (vi) distinguishes mutual simulations from literal SIC isomorphisms; (vii) makes failure-sensitive experimental metrics explicit; and (viii) notes that minimal antichains need not be finite. These are mathematical and specification repairs, \emph{not} reports of new executed experiments.

\textbf{Primary open question.} Can an authorized, resource-accounted Player-0 federation transform a stalled search policy into an accepted settlement, using certified bridge lemmas and controlled adaptive search, at lower fully charged cost than matched alternatives \emph{without} changing the frozen target or confusing an actual first-person event with reachability?

